  "preamble": "Palatalization of the alveolar nasal [n] to [nʲ] before front vowels (or [j]). It is the source of the soft/hard nasal contrast in East Slavic, Baltic and Goidelic, where consonants took on a secondary palatal articulation from a following front vowel.",
